{"type":"finding","severity":"minor","fileName":"docs/work/BANDIT-101/stage3-pm-acceptance.md","codegenInstructions":"Verify each finding against current code. Fix only still-valid issues, skip the rest with a brief reason, keep changes minimal, and validate.\n\nIn @docs/work/BANDIT-101/stage3-pm-acceptance.md around lines 25 - 48, The PM wants concrete test evidence: rerun the four commands shown (node --test test/reviewer-adapters.test.mjs, node --test test/local-qwen-review.test.mjs, node --test test/landing-gates.test.mjs, npm run typecheck) and paste the test summary lines or counts (e.g., \"X tests passed, Y failed\" or the terminal output for each) into the PM Verification section; explicitly confirm that the 7 previously RED tests (the 4 failing cases from test/reviewer-adapters.test.mjs and the 3 from test/landing-gates.test.mjs) are now GREEN by naming the test files and stating their before/after status (e.g., \"test/reviewer-adapters.test.mjs: 4/4 previously failing → all passed (N passed, 0 failed)\"), and include the exact terminal summary or brief snippet for each command as evidence.","suggestions":[]}
{"type":"finding","severity":"major","fileName":"src/state/reviewer-adapters.ts","codegenInstructions":"Verify each finding against current code. Fix only still-valid issues, skip the rest with a brief reason, keep changes minimal, and validate.\n\nIn @src/state/reviewer-adapters.ts around lines 407 - 423, The function readJsonOrEmptyLedger currently treats syntactically-valid but shape-invalid JSON as an empty ledger and thus can silently overwrite real data; change it so that after parsing JSON you validate the shape (using isRecord(parsed) and Array.isArray(parsed.gaps)) and if the shape is invalid throw a descriptive error (e.g. \"malformed bootstrap-gap ledger: missing or invalid 'gaps' array\") instead of returning {version:1,gaps:[]}; keep the existing behavior of only swallowing missing-file errors via isMissingPathError(error) but rethrow any other errors (including shape validation failures) so callers like recordNoReviewerBootstrapGap surface corruption rather than operating on an empty ledger.","suggestions":["async function readJsonOrEmptyLedger(\n  ledgerPath: string\n): Promise<BootstrapGapLedgerShape> {\n  try {\n    const content = await readFile(ledgerPath, \"utf8\");\n    const parsed = JSON.parse(content);\n    if (isRecord(parsed)) {\n      if (!Array.isArray(parsed.gaps)) {\n        throw new Error(\n          `Malformed bootstrap gap ledger: ${ledgerPath} (gaps must be an array)`\n        );\n      }\n      return { version: 1, gaps: parsed.gaps as NoReviewerBootstrapGap[] };\n    }\n    throw new Error(\n      `Malformed bootstrap gap ledger: ${ledgerPath} (root must be an object)`\n    );\n  } catch (error) {\n    if (!isMissingPathError(error)) {\n      throw error;\n    }\n  }\n\n  return { version: 1, gaps: [] };\n}"]}
{"type":"finding","severity":"major","fileName":"test/landing-gates.test.mjs","codegenInstructions":"Verify each finding against current code. Fix only still-valid issues, skip the rest with a brief reason, keep changes minimal, and validate.\n\nIn @test/landing-gates.test.mjs around lines 911 - 933, Add a complementary test to fail-closed when the bootstrap gap ledger declares BANDIT-GAP-NO-REVIEWER-CONFIGURED and no human-review replacement is supplied: in test/landing-gates.test.mjs add a test (mirroring \"land-check accepts human review replacement when bootstrap gap ledger is absent\") that uses createInitializedRepo(), writes a .bandit/bootstrap-gaps.json containing a gap entry for the work (e.g. BANDIT-985 -> \"BANDIT-GAP-NO-REVIEWER-CONFIGURED\"), does NOT call writeHumanReviewEvidence or provide localQwenReplacementEvidence, then call runBandit(repo, [\"land-check\", \"BANDIT-985\"]) and assert the process fails (result.code !== 0) and result.stderr/stdout contains the expected blocking message about missing human review / NO-REVIEWER gap; keep the original test unchanged.","suggestions":["test(\"land-check accepts human review replacement when bootstrap gap ledger is absent\", async () => {\n  const repo = await createInitializedRepo();\n  await rm(path.join(repo, \".bandit/bootstrap-gaps.json\"), { force: true });\n  await initGitRepo(repo);\n  const sourceHead = await commitAll(repo, \"Initial state\");\n  await writeWorkBrief(repo, \"BANDIT-985\", \"Human Review Without Gap Ledger\");\n  await writeHumanReviewEvidence(repo, \"BANDIT-985\", { sourceHead });\n  await writeReviewEvidence(repo, \"BANDIT-985\", {\n    sourceHead,\n    localQwenReplacementEvidence: [\n      \"docs/work/BANDIT-985/human-review.md\"\n    ]\n  });\n  await writeLandingVerdict(repo, \"BANDIT-985\", { sourceHead });\n\n  const result = await runBandit(repo, [\"land-check\", \"BANDIT-985\"]);\n\n  assert.equal(result.code, 0, result.stderr);\n  assert.match(\n    result.stdout,\n    /Human review evidence: docs\\/work\\/BANDIT-985\\/human-review\\.md/\n  );\n});\n\ntest(\"land-check fails closed when no-reviewer gap is declared but ledger is absent and no human replacement exists\", async () => {\n  const repo = await createInitializedRepo();\n  await rm(path.join(repo, \".bandit/bootstrap-gaps.json\"), { force: true });\n  await initGitRepo(repo);\n  const sourceHead = await commitAll(repo, \"Initial state\");\n  await writeWorkBrief(repo, \"BANDIT-986\", \"Declared No Reviewer Gap Without Ledger\");\n  await writeReviewEvidence(repo, \"BANDIT-986\", {\n    sourceHead,\n    bootstrapGaps: [\"BANDIT-GAP-NO-REVIEWER-CONFIGURED\"],\n    localQwenReplacementEvidence: [\"No reviewer is configured for this repository.\"]\n  });\n  await writeLandingVerdict(repo, \"BANDIT-986\", { sourceHead });\n\n  const result = await runBandit(repo, [\"land-check\", \"BANDIT-986\"]);\n  assert.equal(result.code, 1);\n  assert.match(\n    result.stderr,\n    /No reviewer is configured|BANDIT-GAP-NO-REVIEWER-CONFIGURED/\n  );\n});"]}
